          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A vehicle with an 'ard case loses the Open-topped special rule and adds 1 to its Side Armour. It has one Access Point on each side of the hull and one at the rear.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Attack Squig" hidden="false" id="5f90-098a-c9cf-7c99" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Attack Squig" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="3314-def9-e202-000b">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A model with an attack squig adds 1 to its Attacks Characteristic.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Boarding Plank" hidden="false" id="56a9-2e69-4958-ebf6" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Boarding Plank" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="30dd-a390-b9e5-7c87">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">In the Assault phase, if the vehicle is in base contact with an enemy vehicle, one model embarked on it may make its close combat attacks against that vehicle as though it were in base contact.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Bomb Squig" hidden="false" id="1978-a29f-7d13-6fcc" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Bomb Squig" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="ecdf-773b-31ca-7935">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">Once per game, in the Shooting phase, instead of shooting, a unit with a bomb squig may target one enemy Vehicle or Dreadnought within 18". That target suffers one hit at Strength 8, AP 3. Remove the bomb squig after it is used.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Bosspole" hidden="false" id="e2e0-a4e5-4709-03c3" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Bosspole" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="c828-8441-0098-ed5e">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">Once per turn, a unit that includes at least one model with a bosspole may re-roll a failed Morale check or Pinning test. If the re-roll also fails, the unit may still use Breakin' Heads.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Cybork Body" hidden="false" id="db38-ed87-8517-73be" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Cybork Body" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="b6fe-673f-8a03-c960">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A model with a cybork body has the Feel No Pain (6+) special rule. This does not combine with Dok's tools.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Deff Rolla" hidden="false" id="05aa-472d-fcd5-ccd6" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Deff Rolla" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="9319-a345-1855-9230">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">When a vehicle with a deff rolla makes a Ram or Tank Shock, the enemy unit it moves into suffers D6 hits at Strength 10, AP 3.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Dok's Tools" hidden="false" id="bf21-85ba-b63a-bf2c" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Dok's Tools" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="96d5-6981-66fa-895b">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A unit that includes a model with Dok's tools has the Feel No Pain (6+) special rule. A grot orderly improves this by 1.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="'Eavy Armour" hidden="false" id="e4bb-7234-0498-89ca" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="'Eavy Armour" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="7b5b-084d-d861-02b5">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">'Eavy armour confers a 4+ Armour Save.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Gitfinda" hidden="false" id="eeab-d6e7-9c2f-e8a2" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Gitfinda" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="4791-96a0-a9c2-a995">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A model with a gitfinda has a Ballistic Skill of 3 in any turn in which it did not move.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Grabba stikk" hidden="false" id="39d3-bc9b-5ab5-cf59" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Grabba stikk" typeId="1a1a-e592-2849-a5c0" typeName="Weapon" hidden="false" id="354d-16c9-3061-3b0e" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Range" typeId="95ba-cda7-b831-6066">-</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Strength" typeId="24d9-b8e1-a355-2458">User</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="AP" typeId="f7a6-e0d8-7973-cd8d">–</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Type" typeId="2f86-c8b4-b3b4-3ff9">Melee</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Grot-prod" hidden="false" id="cb58-2365-16c2-ecea" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Grot-prod" typeId="1a1a-e592-2849-a5c0" typeName="Weapon" hidden="false" id="1e5b-360c-25a0-1cad" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Range" typeId="95ba-cda7-b831-6066">-</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Strength" typeId="24d9-b8e1-a355-2458">+1</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="AP" typeId="f7a6-e0d8-7973-cd8d">–</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Type" typeId="2f86-c8b4-b3b4-3ff9">Melee</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Grabba Stikk and Grot-prod" hidden="false" id="6317-c7da-09a0-63b9" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Grabba Stikk and Grot-prod" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="8fdd-8ed8-9b8b-c144">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A grabba stikk is a melee weapon (S User, AP –). A grot-prod is a melee weapon (S+1, AP –). While a Runtherd with either lives, his Gretchin unit uses his Leadership of 7 for Morale checks and Pinning tests.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Grabbin' Klaw" hidden="false" id="934d-3535-b930-2d10" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Grabbin' Klaw" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="7ca0-74bf-86cf-9779">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">In the Assault phase, a vehicle with a grabbin' klaw may choose one enemy Vehicle in base contact. Roll a D6; on a 4+, that Vehicle may not move in its next Movement phase.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Grot Oiler" hidden="false" id="9d07-ca90-e7a2-472c" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Grot Oiler" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="daf3-e6e2-9e29-bb1e">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A model with Mek-Smasha and a grot oiler improves its Mek-Smasha (X) by 1, to a best of Mek-Smasha (4+). For example, Mek-Smasha (5+) becomes Mek-Smasha (4+).</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Grot Orderly" hidden="false" id="768a-d615-89d8-8769" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Grot Orderly" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="5b61-bfe8-f048-df9d">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A Painboy with a grot orderly improves the Feel No Pain (X) from his Dok's tools by 1. For example, Feel No Pain (6+) becomes Feel No Pain (5+).</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Grot Riggers" hidden="false" id="681c-0e52-a80a-61fe" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Grot Riggers" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="69d5-9971-ece4-fa00">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">An Ork vehicle with grot riggers gains Grot Riggers (6+). An Ork Dreadnought with grot riggers instead gains the It Will Not Die special rule. A Knight that takes grot riggers gains Grot Riggers (5+).</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="It Will Not Die (X)" id="4a90-5c48-298b-1ead" hidden="false" targetId="2784-d0be-a4e2-890f" type="rule">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" field="name" value="It Will Not Die" />
          </modifiers>
        </infoLink>
      </infoLinks>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Kustom Force Field" hidden="false" id="2579-9744-3dac-8284" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Kustom Force Field" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="c89d-619b-5b79-cac9">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">Friendly units wholly within 6" of a model with a kustom force field have a 5+ Invulnerable Save against Shooting Attacks. Other vehicles within range count as obscured instead. A Knight or Titan carrying a kustom force field has the 5+ Invulnerable Save against Shooting Attacks itself.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Mega Armour" hidden="false" id="8d14-6802-9cee-9a7f" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Mega Armour" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="f6f1-ddcb-f7a1-7f0c">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">Mega armour confers a 2+ Armour Save. A model with the Infantry Unit Type that takes mega armour gains the Heavy Unit Sub-type, changes its Movement Characteristic to 5, and may not Advance.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Da Finkin' Kap" hidden="false" id="31da-a322-2edb-e599" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <constraints>
        <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" shared="true" id="8f0b-e6f6-f637-02b1" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
      </constraints>
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Da Finkin' Kap" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="6bff-aca1-b8d4-7c06">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">Warboss or Big Mek. If the bearer is your Warlord, he may choose two generic Warlord Traits instead of one</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Da Fixxerupperz" hidden="false" id="60b0-93e9-b002-5ea8" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <constraints>
        <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" shared="true" id="fcf6-14c7-c919-44f0" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
      </constraints>
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Da Fixxerupperz" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="18f9-23b3-c715-d4b3">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">Big Mek only. The bearer's Mek-Smasha improves by 1, and he may use it twice each turn</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Da Killa Klaw" hidden="false" id="c5f6-0f57-6bfd-cdff" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <constraints>
        <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" shared="true" id="5304-0e19-846b-906a" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
      </constraints>
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Da Killa Klaw" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="d4d2-c8a6-e4a4-7576">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">Warboss or Big Mek. Replaces his power klaw: melee, S x2, AP 2, Unwieldy, Shred; the bearer may re-roll failed to-wound rolls</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Da Lucky Stikk" hidden="false" id="116e-ee17-d3a3-ebda" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <constraints>
        <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" shared="true" id="f8c3-6ff7-05d8-854c" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
      </constraints>
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Da Lucky Stikk" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="535e-69a5-9278-6068">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">Warboss or Big Mek. The bearer and any unit he joins add 1 to their Leadership and may re-roll to-hit rolls of 1 in close combat</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Headwoppa's Killchoppa" hidden="false" id="2de6-6918-9046-7c8d" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <constraints>
        <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" shared="true" id="838e-8ec1-ad20-8278" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
      </constraints>
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Headwoppa's Killchoppa" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="d733-45ad-19ac-3866">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">Warboss or Big Mek. Replaces his choppa: melee, S+2, AP 4, Murderous Strike (6+)</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Warboss Gazbag's Blitzbike" hidden="false" id="06a0-9bdd-1a53-33f6" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <constraints>
        <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" shared="true" id="7eda-0372-7319-cabe" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
      </constraints>
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Warboss Gazbag's Blitzbike" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="cc70-cff1-1d7d-b579">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">Warboss on warbike only. His twin-linked big shoota gains Shred, and he has Shrouded (4+) in a turn in which he Advanced</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Red Paint Job" hidden="false" id="c40e-efd7-b51e-395a" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Red Paint Job" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="2f76-4cec-ddc5-d9e6">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A vehicle with a red paint job adds 1 to its Movement Characteristic. This stacks with Red Ones Go Fasta.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Reinforced Ram" hidden="false" id="f0d3-a0b3-3516-ec85" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Reinforced Ram" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="e444-e27e-a3d3-b08d">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A vehicle with a reinforced ram may re-roll failed Dangerous Terrain tests and adds 1 to its Strength when Ramming.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Rokk-pack" hidden="false" id="7132-a555-3981-3cc3" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Rokk-pack" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="397b-c5ad-3be9-3e61">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">At the start of the controlling player's Movement phase, or when deployed as part of a Deep Strike Assault, a model with a rokk-pack may set its Move Characteristic to 12 for the duration of the controlling player's turn ("activating" the rokk-pack). This lets it move up to 12", regardless of the Movement Characteristic on its profile, and gain any other benefits of a Movement Characteristic of 12, including the bonus to Charge distance. A model with an activated rokk-pack ignores terrain while Moving and Charging, but must take Dangerous Terrain tests as normal when beginning or ending its move in Dangerous Terrain; it treats all Difficult Terrain as Dangerous Terrain, and may move over friendly and enemy models or units without penalty, but must end its move at least 1" away from any model from another unit. A model with a rokk-pack may still Advance if it would normally be able to (this does not allow units that include any models with the Heavy sub-type to Advance). When it Advances with an activated rokk-pack, add its Initiative Characteristic to 12 to determine how far it may move; it ignores terrain and models from other units while doing so, but may not make Shooting Attacks or declare a Charge in the same turn, as per the normal rules for Advancing. Any model with a rokk-pack also gains the Bulky (2), Hammer of Wrath (1) and Deep Strike special rules; if it already has Bulky (2), it gains Bulky (3) instead. During a Reaction made in any phase, a player may not activate a model's rokk-pack to gain any bonus to its Movement Characteristic. Models with rokk-packs deployed as part of a Deep Strike Assault are considered to have activated their rokk-packs in the turn they enter play.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Squig Hound" hidden="false" id="95d9-0a4c-52a0-f977" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Squig Hound" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="df84-79c6-7598-d7f6">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A Gretchin unit whose Runtherd has a squig hound may re-roll failed Morale checks.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Stikkbomb Chukka" hidden="false" id="e541-8b6e-8df8-3b12" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Stikkbomb Chukka" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="81be-ff09-180b-a217">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">Units disembarking from a vehicle with a stikkbomb chukka count as having stikkbombz when they charge in the same turn.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Stikkbombz" hidden="false" id="960a-b583-75a7-cab5" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Stikkbombz" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="402d-9eb8-e4a2-4e62">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">Stikkbombz count as frag grenades†.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Tankbusta Bombz" hidden="false" id="13d1-b389-4f9a-4f6f" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Tankbusta Bombz" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="3f06-5ada-19f5-96f3">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">Tankbusta bombz count as melta bombs†.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Tellyporta" hidden="false" id="01f3-497d-aa7d-c658" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Tellyporta" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="f17c-8cb4-4dad-4644">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A model with a tellyporta, and any unit it joins, gains the Deep Strike special rule. A model with a warbike may not take a tellyporta.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="Deep Strike" id="6498-5322-9dc0-a847" hidden="false" targetId="f1e1-986f-c783-ca9e" type="rule" />
      </infoLinks>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Waaagh! Banner" hidden="false" id="cced-0024-06cc-b831" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Waaagh! Banner" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="7c7e-35b7-82f7-351a">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A unit that includes at least one model with a Waaagh! banner adds 1 to its Weapon Skill while that model lives.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Warbike" hidden="false" id="75f2-0220-1fb3-60d2" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Warbike" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="dd43-fdec-1a36-4ccb">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A warbike has a twin-linked big shoota. A model with the Infantry Unit Type that selects a warbike as an upgrade must change its Unit Type to Cavalry, keeping any Unit Sub-types it previously had. It also changes its Movement Characteristic to 14, adds 1 to its Toughness, has a 4+ Armour Save, and gains the Hammer of Wrath (1) special rule. In addition, a model with a warbike that chooses to Advance gains the Shrouded (5+) special rule until the start of the controlling player's next turn.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="Hammer of Wrath (X)" id="343e-3e5b-e2d3-e280" hidden="false" targetId="aec0-c3aa-1e4e-1779" type="rule">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" field="name" value="Hammer of Wrath (1)" />
          </modifiers>
        </infoLink>
      </infoLinks>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Wreckin' Ball" hidden="false" id="9896-1609-46e7-100a" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Wreckin' Ball" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="a840-42b2-d717-0b63">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">In the Assault phase, a vehicle with a wreckin' ball may make one melee attack at Strength 8, AP 4 against an enemy unit in base contact.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Da Jump" hidden="false" id="920b-c0d6-3639-f13b" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Da Jump" typeId="5405-b3c6-e8d0-4e77" typeName="Psychic Power" hidden="false" id="c4a7-5d44-e69f-5155">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="4c0f-7e2f-586c-9305">Movement phase. Select one friendly Ork unit within 12" of the Weirdboy, plus one more for each +1 of his current Waaagh! Energy bonus. Remove the selected units from the battlefield and place them in Reserves. Roll for them as normal for Reserves, adding the Waaagh! Energy bonus to each roll; when they arrive, they enter play by Deep Strike as normal. The Waaagh! Energy bonus is fixed when Da Jump is cast, and that same value is used for these Reserves rolls.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Fists of Gork" hidden="false" id="984c-272d-334e-5a2a" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Fists of Gork" typeId="5405-b3c6-e8d0-4e77" typeName="Psychic Power" hidden="false" id="1ecc-87cc-c0e0-b67b">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="4c0f-7e2f-586c-9305">Assault phase. Until end of phase the Weirdboy has +2 Strength and +2 Attacks.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="Beastboss" hidden="false" id="f037-60e3-2394-0e3d" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <rules>
        <rule name="Beastboss" id="34f4-d16f-41c8-c05d" hidden="false">
          <description>May only join Beast Snagga Boyz; while he lives, that unit has Feel No Pain (6+) and re-rolls charge distance</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <infoLinks>
