  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Mob Rule" id="9986-6062-e065-6f8a" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>Orks draw courage and fury from their numbers. A unit with this rule gains the following, counting the models in the unit at the time: Unit Size: Leadership, Furious Charge. 1–9: No bonus, None. 10–19: +1, Furious Charge (1). 20–29: +2, Furious Charge (2). 30 or more: +3, Furious Charge (2). Furious Charge: the unit gains Furious Charge (1) for every full 10 models, to a maximum of Furious Charge (2). If it already has Furious Charge (X), use whichever value is higher. Leadership: the unit adds +1 to its Leadership for every full 10 models, to a maximum of +3. Its Leadership can never be raised above 10 this way. Orderly Charge: the unit's charges are never Disorderly Charges†, however many units it charges.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Breakin' Heads" id="740a-e433-bb54-c49d" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>If a unit with Mob Rule that includes a Nob, Boss Nob or Ork character fails a Morale check or Pinning test, it may choose to pass it instead. If it does, the unit suffers D3 automatic hits at Strength 6, AP –, allocated by the Ork player to models other than characters; armour saves may be taken.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="'Ere We Go!" id="fe04-50c9-c0ad-8fb5" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>When rolling charge distance, the unit may re-roll one of the dice. If the charge still fails, the unit moves the full distance rolled toward the target, instead of the usual reduced failed-charge move†.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Waaagh!" id="01d0-45ce-18b3-5564" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>Once per game, at the start of your turn, if your Warlord is an Ork and is on the table, you may call a Waaagh! Until the end of that turn, every unit with this rule gains the following: Fleet (+1): the unit gains Fleet (1), or increases an existing Fleet (X) by 1. Furious Charge (+1): the unit gains Furious Charge (1), or increases an existing Furious Charge (X) by 1. Units with Mob Rule also automatically pass Morale checks until the start of your next turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Grot Riggers (X)" id="b62c-5ed8-63f2-5b53" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>At the end of each of your turns, roll a D6 for each model with this rule that has lost Hull Points. On a roll of X or more, it restores one lost Hull Point, up to its starting value. A model cannot use Grot Riggers in a turn it was embarked, Falling Back or locked in combat†.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Grot 'Tendant" id="a26d-6630-480f-550c" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>A model with this rule is an attendant grot in its owner's unit. It does not count towards the unit's size, never gains Klan (X), and may not issue, accept or be chosen for a challenge. Hits can only be allocated to it by attacks with Precision Shots or Precision Strikes. When a Wound would be allocated to another model in its unit, the controlling player may allocate that Wound to a model with this rule instead. If it is removed, any bonus it gives is lost.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Mek-Smasha (X)" id="6989-913d-92e6-2a8b" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>If a model with the Mek-Smasha (X) special rule is in base contact with, or Embarked upon, one or more damaged Vehicles, Dreadnoughts, Automata, or Mechanized units during the Shooting phase, they can attempt to repair one of them. If they do so, the model that attempted the repair cannot shoot any weapons or use any other abilities that would be used instead of making a Shooting Attack. Roll a D6. If the result is equal to or more than the value listed in brackets as part of this rule, the repair is successful. Apply one of the following options to the target unit the model is in base contact with or Embarked upon: Repair a Weapon Destroyed result. Repair an Immobilised result. Restore a lost Hull Point. Restore a lost Wound. If a Weapon Destroyed result is repaired, that weapon may not be used to attack in the same phase as it is repaired, but may be used to attack as normal in any phase after that. The Mek-Smasha cannot use this ability if they are Pinned or Falling Back.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Mob size" id="d187-868d-395c-5256" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>Units with Mob Rule never gain the Fearless special rule from any source, including characters who join them. This keeps Breakin' Heads meaningful.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ramshackle (X)" id="a24d-bb55-ef95-085b" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>When an Ork vehicle with this rule suffers a penetrating hit, roll a D6 before rolling on the Vehicle Damage table†. On a roll of X or more, the hit is treated as a glancing hit instead. Knights and Titans have Ramshackle (5+); all other Ork vehicles have Ramshackle (6+). On a model with a Wounds Characteristic (such as the Speed Freek buggies), Ramshackle (X) is a damage mitigation rule instead: each time the model would lose a Wound, roll a D6; on a roll of X or more, that Wound is not lost. Ramshackle is not Feel No Pain: rules that ignore or negate Feel No Pain do not affect it. It is a Damage Mitigation roll: a model may make only a single Damage Mitigation roll of any type (including Feel No Pain) for any given Wound.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Stealth" id="4f86-aae1-17da-67cb" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>If the model has not moved this turn, it cannot be targeted by ranged attacks from more than 12" away.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Waaagh! Energy" id="22d5-a04c-eb29-712d" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>When a Weirdboy makes a Psychic check, count the friendly Ork models within 12" of him. He gains +1 Leadership for every full 10 models, to a maximum of +3. His Leadership can never be raised above 10 by this rule. The power of the Waaagh! is hard to control: an Ork Psychic check suffers Perils of the Warp on any double, even if the check is passed. Every Weirdboy knows the first two entries. A Weirdboy with the Warphead upgrade also knows Fists of Gork. Power: Kind, Phase, Effect. Da Jump: Psychic power, Movement, Select one friendly Ork unit within 12" of the Weirdboy, plus one more for each +1 of his current Waaagh! Energy bonus. Remove the selected units from the battlefield and place them in Reserves. Roll for them as normal for Reserves, adding the Waaagh! Energy bonus to each roll; when they arrive, they enter play by Deep Strike as normal. The Waaagh! Energy bonus is fixed when Da Jump is cast, and that same value is used for these Reserves rolls.. Fists of Gork: Psychic power, Assault, Until end of phase the Weirdboy has +2 Strength and +2 Attacks.. Frazzle: Psychic weapon, Shooting, Template, S5, AP4, Assault 1, Pinning.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Klan (X)" id="a734-620c-db79-3594" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>When building an army, choose one Klan for its Primary Detachment; an Allied Detachment may choose a different Klan. Every unit in that detachment with the Mob Rule special rule, and every Ork vehicle and Dreadnought, gains Klan (X), where X is the chosen Klan. Gretchin units and Gretchin crew never gain Klan (X).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Invulnerable Save (X)" id="85f3-c187-c717-378e" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>The model has an Invulnerable Save of X, which may be taken against any Wound instead of its armour save.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Tank Hunters" id="cb2f-190f-9b7f-0f1e" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>Listed on this datasheet but not defined in the conversion doc.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Open-topped" id="792a-d019-9e41-d7f8" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>Listed on this datasheet but not defined in the conversion doc.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
